What:		/sys/devices/platform/[0-9]+.dpa/dma_alloc
Date:		May 2025
KernelVersion:	6.12
Contact:	koudai@google.com
Description:	Allocates a pair of DMA buffers (src and dst) for the DPA to operate on

		Write:
		Accepts the size of the buffer to allocate. Allocates two DMA buffers of the given
		size, and a subdirectory dma_buffer_N with further functions to operate on those
		buffers (where N is the number of times this interface has been called)

		Example usage:

		$ echo 5 > dma_alloc
		$ cd dma_buffer_0
		$ echo "test" > src_buf
		$ echo 1 > ncp_memcpy
		$ cat dst_buf
		test

