What:		/sys/devices/platform/[0-9]+.dpa/ipsec/pusher/data
Date:		June 2025
KernelVersion:	6.12
Contact:	bgillon@google.com
Description:	Send data over to IPSec tester service.

		Write:
		Accepts at least 4 bytes. The first 4 bytes are representing
		a big endian number that is the size of the data to be pushed.
		The next bytes are the data to be transferred into the IPSec
		tester service.
		Returns negative error code on error, 0 on success.

		Example usage:

		$ echo -en "\x00\x00\x00\x05\x01\x02\x03\x04\x05" > data

What:		/sys/devices/platform/[0-9]+.dpa/ipsec/pusher/status
Date:		June 2025
KernelVersion:	6.12
Contact:	bgillon@google.com
Description:	Read the current status of the IPSec tester service.

		The status will be one of:

		- "Idle"
		- "InProgress"
		- "CompletedOK"
		- "Error"
		- "PendingData"
		- "Unknown State (<ERROR_CODE>)"

		"Idle" means the driver is ready for a new data
		transfer

		"InProgress" means all the data is being transmitted.
		While in progress, no data should be send to the driver

		"CompletedOk" means the data transfer was successful.
		A new data transfer is possible.

		"Error" means the driver encountered an error

		"PendingData" means the driver is waiting for more data

		"Unknown State (<ERROR_CODE>)" means the driver ended up in an
		unknown state

		Example usage:

		$ cat status
		CompletedOK
